## ✍ DM Response
In the heart of Broceliande, where ancient oaks entwine to form a verdant canopy overhead, Peredur map Gwrtheyrn sought solace amidst the whispering leaves. His eyes, though filled with unyielding determination, were tinged with fatigue and doubt - the weight of an ancestral quest bearing down upon him like the gnarled roots beneath his feet.

Calling forth the power of his devotion, Peredur closed his eyes and felt a surge of energy coursing through his veins. The world seemed to shift around him, growing brighter as though the very light itself was bending to his will. A halo formed around him, shimmering with an otherworldly glow that seemed almost too real to touch.

The forest stirred in response, as if sensing the divine presence within Peredur. The air filled with the faint echoes of ancient voices, murmuring tales of forgotten heroes and lost treasures. He could hear whispers of his ancestor Percival's quest for the Grail, each one a testament to the power that coursed through their shared bloodline.

As the halo began to fade, Peredur felt a renewed sense of purpose wash over him. The doubts and fears that had plagued him since arriving in Broceliande seemed to dissipate like morning mist before the summer sun. He knew then, with unshakable certainty, that he was on the right path.

The forest seemed to acknowledge his newfound resolve, as if bestowing a silent blessing upon him. The whispers grew softer, fading away until only the gentle rustle of leaves could be heard once more. Peredur opened his eyes, feeling stronger than ever before and ready to face whatever challenges lay ahead on his quest for the Grail.

Yet even as he turned to continue his search, there was a sense of unease gnawing at him. The forest, though peaceful now, still held many secrets - secrets that might not be so welcoming should they reveal themselves. But Peredur steeled himself against such thoughts, knowing that the only way forward was through.

With renewed determination, he stepped back onto the path and ventured deeper into Broceliande, guided by the divine power of his devotion and the echoes of his ancestor's quest. The journey ahead would be long and fraught with danger, but Peredur had already faced far greater trials than this - and emerged victorious each time.

## 📋 Summary
Peredur map Gwrtheyrn summoned ancient power within Broceliande's forest, causing a halo to form around him and stirring whispers of ancestral tales. His doubts subsided, granting him newfound purpose and a silent blessing from the forest. However, an underlying sense of unease persisted as he continued his quest for the Grail.
